4. Liquidity Reserve

Allocation

50 Billion EXO

Current Supply Status

5 Billion EXO have been supplied as initial liquidity through Uniswap V4.
Remaining liquidity reserve: 45 Billion EXO.

Operating Principles

The remaining liquidity reserve will not be supplied immediately.
Additional liquidity may be considered depending on community activity and project growth.
If additional liquidity is deemed necessary, the operating team will disclose the following information in advance:

• Purpose of supply
• Amount of supply
• Timing of supply
• Expected impact

Final approval will be determined through community discussion and voting.

Core Principle

Liquidity additions will be conducted gradually through communication and voting with the community.
Liquidity supply will not be used as a tool to artificially manipulate market prices.
5. Founder Allocation

Allocation

10 Billion EXO
Founder Allocation Wallet:
0x3f360a0Cb2713f750F8E8C80900feCc6A841993d

Initial Operating Principle

Founder allocation tokens are intended to remain unused for two years from the token creation date.
During this period, the founder voluntarily commits to holding these tokens and not using them for personal gain or discretionary sale or transfer.
This policy is based on the founder’s publicly declared operating principles and is not enforced through a smart-contract lock mechanism.

Exceptional Circumstances

Limited use may occur under the following conditions:

• A significant threat to project survival
• Unforeseen market risks
• Emergency actions required to protect the ecosystem

After the two-year period, any use of founder allocation tokens will be publicly disclosed, discussed with the community, and executed only with consideration for market stability.
In such cases, the operating team will provide prior notice to the community and seek to minimize any potential market impact.

Availability Date

October 19, 2028, 08:59:42 UTC

Core Principle

Founder allocation tokens are not assets intended for short-term profit realization.
The founder prioritizes the long-term growth and stability of the project.
6. Defense Reserve

Allocation

25 Billion EXO
• 5 dedicated wallets
• 5 Billion EXO allocated to each wallet

Purpose

The Defense Reserve serves as an emergency asset dedicated to protecting the EXO ecosystem and maintaining stability.

Prohibited Uses

The Defense Reserve shall not be used for:

• Personal gain of operators
• Founder compensation
• Development expenses
• Operational expenses
• Marketing expenses
• Investment recovery
• General business costs
• Any use unrelated to ecosystem defense

Usage Procedure

When use of the Defense Reserve becomes necessary, the operating team will disclose:

• Purpose of use
• Amount used
• Time of use
• Expected effect

Community discussion and voting will follow before execution.

Emergency Exception

Execution may precede disclosure in cases such as:

• Project survival threats
• Malicious attacks
• Liquidity crises
• Abnormal market conditions
• Other situations requiring immediate action

Following emergency actions, the operating team will disclose:

• Purpose of use
• Amount used
• Time of use
• Results achieved

Core Declaration

The 25 Billion EXO Defense Reserve exists solely for ecosystem protection.
Use for any other purpose is strictly prohibited.
7. Development & Operations Fund

Allocation

15 Billion EXO
• 5 dedicated wallets
• 3 Billion EXO allocated to each wallet

Intended Uses

• Platform development
• System maintenance
• Server operations
• Security enhancements
• Community management
• Marketing and promotion
• Partnership development
• Other activities supporting project growth

Disclosure Policy

The operating team will disclose:
• Purpose of use
• Amount used
• Date of use
• Details of expenditure

Core Principle

The Development & Operations Fund exists to support the project’s growth and sustainability.
If prior disclosure could jeopardize operational security, execution may occur before disclosure.
All usage records are intended to be disclosed transparently.
8. Governance Policy

This policy establishes the operational principles intended to support transparency, stability, and long-term decentralization within the EXO ecosystem.
EXO prioritizes transparency and accountability regarding token supply and smart-contract administrative authority.
9. Community Voting Policy

Voting Subjects

The following matters are generally subject to community voting:

• Additional minting
• Token burning
• Additional liquidity supply
• Defense Reserve usage
• Significant tokenomics changes
• Major policy changes
• Other matters deemed important by the operating team

Voting Announcement

The following information will be disclosed before voting:

• Proposal details
• Purpose
• Expected benefits
• Anticipated impact
• Voting start date
• Voting end date

Voting Period

Voting periods will be determined separately according to the urgency and significance of each proposal.

Approval Requirement

Approval: 50.1% or more of valid votes cast.
Rejection: Less than 50.1% of valid votes cast.

Result Disclosure

The operating team will disclose:
• Total participants
• Votes in favor
• Votes against
• Abstentions (if applicable)
• Final approval percentage
• Approval or rejection outcome

Core Principle

The operating team will respect voting results and seek to reflect the will of the community.
10. Minting Policy

The EXO smart contract currently contains minting functionality.
However, the project's default principle is not to conduct additional minting.
Minting authority is retained solely for circumstances such as:

• Token migration
• Chain migration
• Token swaps
• Ecosystem restructuring
• Other special cases approved by the community

No additional minting will occur without community approval.
11. Burning Policy

The EXO smart contract currently contains burn functionality.
However, the project's default principle is not to conduct discretionary token burning.
Any burn proposal will follow the process below:

• Public disclosure of necessity
• Disclosure of burn amount
• Disclosure of expected effects
• Disclosure of implementation schedule
• Community discussion
• Community voting

All burn records will be publicly verifiable on-chain.
12. Ownership Policy

EXO currently maintains smart-contract ownership.

Ownership represents the minimum administrative authority required for operation, maintenance, and technical stability.
Ownership is not intended for supply manipulation or market intervention.
Ownership actions will be disclosed to the community whenever reasonably possible.
13. Renounce Ownership Policy

EXO has not renounced ownership at this time.
The operating team does not intend to maintain ownership permanently.
Ownership renunciation may be considered after project stabilization and sufficient community discussion.
14. Transparency Declaration

✅ No routine minting
✅ No routine burning
✅ Advance disclosure of major policies
✅ Community discussion prioritized
✅ Voting-based decision making
✅ Public on-chain records
✅ Transparent operational disclosures
✅ Commitment to long-term decentralization
15. Risk Disclosure

EXO does not guarantee price appreciation or financial returns.
This whitepaper is not intended as investment advice or an offer to invest.
Cryptocurrency markets are highly volatile and may result in partial or complete loss of capital.
All investment decisions and participation are undertaken at the sole responsibility of each participant.
16. Final Declaration

EXO chooses transparent operations over exaggerated promises.
EXO does not sell an unrealized future.
EXO operates according to the policies and principles publicly disclosed today.
The operating team does not seek to mislead the community with unconfirmed plans and accepts responsibility for all publicly disclosed information.

All policies and token usage records can be independently verified through public disclosures and on-chain records.
EXO does not ask for trust. We believe in providing verifiable information.
We do not promise the future.
We disclose our principles today.
And we act according to those principles.
